WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.917 --> 00:00:02.699
- [Narrator] Before there was this guy,

00:00:02.699 --> 00:00:04.384
there was this guy.

00:00:04.384 --> 00:00:06.549
A rich flamboyant media titan who wanted

00:00:06.549 --> 00:00:09.909
nothing more than to be
President of the United States.

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:14.076
He was basically Donald
Trump before Donald Trump.

00:00:17.906 --> 00:00:21.255
Bernard McFadden, born August 16, 1868.

00:00:21.255 --> 00:00:23.197
Later changed his name to Bernarr

00:00:23.197 --> 00:00:25.117
because he thought it made him sound more

00:00:25.117 --> 00:00:27.165
like a lion's roar.

00:00:27.165 --> 00:00:28.669
Made his money in
publishing and became known

00:00:28.669 --> 00:00:31.143
as one of the Godfather's of the tableau.

00:00:31.143 --> 00:00:32.647
So naturally, he plastered his face

00:00:32.647 --> 00:00:34.757
all over his magazines.

00:00:34.757 --> 00:00:37.957
But Bernarr's real passion was fitness.

00:00:37.957 --> 00:00:39.984
He fashioned himself a personal trainer

00:00:39.984 --> 00:00:42.928
and spawned a religion, Cosmotarianism,

00:00:42.928 --> 00:00:44.666
which blended his wacky health theories

00:00:44.666 --> 00:00:45.776
with the Bible.

00:00:45.776 --> 00:00:47.418
He was married four times.

00:00:47.418 --> 00:00:49.370
One wife was 26 years his junior,

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:50.870
another nearly 40.

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:53.594
But things really get interesting

00:00:53.594 --> 00:00:55.696
when Bernarr gets into politics.

00:00:55.696 --> 00:00:57.530
He started by campaigning for the creation

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:00.517
of a new position named
the Secretary of Health.

00:01:00.517 --> 00:01:02.042
Bernarr didn't get the job.

00:01:02.042 --> 00:01:03.461
So he aimed higher.

00:01:03.461 --> 00:01:06.269
In 1936 he ran for President boasting that

00:01:06.269 --> 00:01:07.997
all illegal and poor immigrants should be

00:01:07.997 --> 00:01:09.778
shipped back to their homelands.

00:01:09.778 --> 00:01:11.464
Sound familiar?

00:01:11.464 --> 00:01:13.277
He didn't get the Republican nomination.

00:01:13.277 --> 00:01:14.984
So he tried again.

00:01:14.984 --> 00:01:16.562
This time he ran as a democrat in Florida

00:01:16.562 --> 00:01:18.290
for a seat in the U.S. Senate.

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:19.410
He didn't win.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:21.714
Then, he ran for Mayor of New York City,

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:24.178
but he wasn't even allowed on the ballot.

00:01:24.178 --> 00:01:25.768
Though he never won any election

00:01:25.768 --> 00:01:27.645
and eventually ran out of money,

00:01:27.645 --> 00:01:29.821
his quest for fame never died.

00:01:29.821 --> 00:01:31.976
For his 84th birthday, he parachuted out

00:01:31.976 --> 00:01:34.770
of an airplane in Paris.

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:37.270
(jazzy music)

